IMPORT `uc-core-bodies`
IMPORT `uc2-domain`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Part 7 (THE BENEFIT CAP): regulations 78 to 83.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (lines 1265-1358), a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the official text.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Money is a NUMBER of pounds; a calculated amount is rounded once, at the end, with the keel's
-- `core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny` (regulation 6(1)), except the regulation 82(1)(a) earnings threshold, which
-- regulation 6(1A)(za) rounds down to a whole pound (`core — an amount with any fraction of a pound disregarded`).
--
-- Regulation 79 is the rule that says whether the cap applies; it asks (a) whether the welfare benefits exceed the relevant amount
-- (regulations 80 and 80A), (b) whether regulation 82 (earnings) applies, and (c) whether regulation 83 (certain benefits) applies.
-- Regulation 81 then says by how much the universal credit is reduced.

§ `Part 7 -- The benefit cap`

§§ `Part heading and regulation 78(1) -- Introduction (inert)`
-- src:1265 | PART 7 — THE BENEFIT CAP
-- src:1266 | 78 Introduction
-- src:1267 | (1) This Part makes provision for a benefit cap under section 96 of the Act which, if applicable, reduces the amount of an award of universal credit.
-- INERT: the Part heading and a statement of what the Part is for. It cites section 96 of the Act (the benefit cap), which is not an
-- input, and decides nothing a person could ask.

§§ `Regulation 78(2) -- "couple"`

-- src:1268 | (2) In this Part “couple” means—
-- src:1269 | (a) joint claimants; or
-- src:1270 | (b) a single claimant who is a member of a couple within the meaning of section 39 of the Act and the other member of that couple,
-- src:1271 | and references to a couple include each member of that couple individually.
@ref reg 78(2) (src:1268-1271)
GIVEN basis IS A `Claim basis`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 78(2) — the claim is by a couple` basis MEANS
    CONSIDER basis
    WHEN `a single claimant` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Regulation 79 -- Circumstances where the benefit cap applies`

-- Paragraph (2): the reference period is the assessment period for an award of universal credit.
-- src:1274 | (2) The reference period for the purposes of the benefit cap is the assessment period for an award of universal credit.
@ref reg 79(2) (src:1274)
GIVEN period IS AN `Assessment period`
GIVETH AN `Assessment period`
`reg 79(2) — the reference period` period MEANS period

-- Paragraph (1): unless regulation 82 or 83 applies, the cap applies where the welfare benefits to which a single person or couple
-- is entitled during the reference period exceed the relevant amount determined under regulation 80A. (79(3) and (4) are runs of
-- dots in this text.)
-- src:1272 | 79 Circumstances where the benefit cap applies
-- src:1273 | (1) Unless regulation 82 or 83 applies, the benefit cap applies where the welfare benefits to which a single person or couple is entitled during the reference period exceed the relevant amount determined under regulation 80A (relevant amount).
@ref reg 79(1) (src:1272-1273)
GIVEN `total welfare benefits to which the single person or couple is entitled during the reference period` IS A NUMBER
      `relevant amount determined under regulation 80A` IS A NUMBER
      `regulation 82 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 83 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 79(1) — the benefit cap applies` `total welfare benefits to which the single person or couple is entitled during the reference period` `relevant amount determined under regulation 80A` `regulation 82 applies` `regulation 83 applies` MEANS
        (NOT `regulation 82 applies`)
    AND (NOT `regulation 83 applies`)
    AND (`total welfare benefits to which the single person or couple is entitled during the reference period` GREATER THAN `relevant amount determined under regulation 80A`)

§§ `Regulation 79(3) and (4) -- repealed or blank in this text`
-- src:1275 | (3) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:1276 | (4) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- The two lines are runs of dots: repealed paragraphs. The lettering is kept and nothing is filled in.

§§ `Regulation 80 -- Manner of determining total entitlement to welfare benefits`

-- src:1277 | 80 Manner of determining total entitlement to welfare benefits
-- src:1278 | (1) Subject to the following provisions of this regulation, the amount of a welfare benefit to be used when determining total entitlement to welfare benefits is the amount to which the single person or couple is entitled during the reference period subject to any adjustment to the amount payable in accordance with regulations under section 73 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992 (overlapping benefits).
-- src:1279 | (2) Where the welfare benefit is universal credit, the amount to be used is the amount to which the claimant is entitled before any reduction under regulation 81 or under section 26 or 27 of the Act.
-- src:1280 | (2A) Where the welfare benefit is housing benefit under section 130 of the Contributions and Benefits Act, the amount to be used is nil.
-- src:1281 | (3) Where a person is disqualified for receiving an employment and support allowance by virtue of section 18 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007, it is disregarded as a welfare benefit.
-- src:1282 | (4) Where an amount of a welfare benefit is taken into account in assessing a single person's or a couple's unearned income for the purposes of an award of universal credit the amount to be used is the amount taken into account as unearned income in accordance with regulation 66.
-- src:1283 | (5) Where a welfare benefit is awarded in respect of a period that is not a month, the amount is to be calculated as the monthly equivalent as set out in regulation 73 (unearned income calculated monthly).
@ref reg 80 (src:1277-1283)
DECLARE `Kind of welfare benefit for regulation 80` IS ONE OF
    `universal credit`
    `housing benefit under section 130 of the Contributions and Benefits Act`
    `employment and support allowance for which the person is disqualified by virtue of section 18 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007`
    `another welfare benefit`

-- src:1277 | 80 Manner of determining total entitlement to welfare benefits
-- src:1278 | (1) Subject to the following provisions of this regulation, the amount of a welfare benefit to be used when determining total entitlement to welfare benefits is the amount to which the single person or couple is entitled during the reference period subject to any adjustment to the amount payable in accordance with regulations under section 73 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992 (overlapping benefits).
-- src:1279 | (2) Where the welfare benefit is universal credit, the amount to be used is the amount to which the claimant is entitled before any reduction under regulation 81 or under section 26 or 27 of the Act.
-- src:1280 | (2A) Where the welfare benefit is housing benefit under section 130 of the Contributions and Benefits Act, the amount to be used is nil.
-- src:1281 | (3) Where a person is disqualified for receiving an employment and support allowance by virtue of section 18 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007, it is disregarded as a welfare benefit.
-- src:1282 | (4) Where an amount of a welfare benefit is taken into account in assessing a single person's or a couple's unearned income for the purposes of an award of universal credit the amount to be used is the amount taken into account as unearned income in accordance with regulation 66.
-- src:1283 | (5) Where a welfare benefit is awarded in respect of a period that is not a month, the amount is to be calculated as the monthly equivalent as set out in regulation 73 (unearned income calculated monthly).
@ref reg 80 (src:1277-1283)
DECLARE `Welfare benefit to which a person or couple is entitled during the reference period` HAS
    kind                                                                                      IS A `Kind of welfare benefit for regulation 80`
    `amount to which the person or couple is entitled for the period for which the benefit is awarded, after any adjustment in accordance with regulations under section 73 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992`  IS A NUMBER
    `interval of the period for which the benefit is awarded`                                 IS A `Payment interval`
    `amount of universal credit to which the claimant is entitled before any reduction under regulation 81 or under section 26 or 27 of the Act`  IS A NUMBER
    `amount taken into account as unearned income in accordance with regulation 66`           IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- Paragraph (1): the amount to which the person or couple is entitled during the reference period, subject to any adjustment for
-- overlapping benefits (section 73 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992, a stated input). Paragraph (5): a benefit awarded
-- for a period that is not a month is brought to its monthly equivalent as regulation 73 provides (the keel's table). Paragraph (4):
-- where an amount of a welfare benefit is taken into account as unearned income, that amount is used. Paragraph (2): for universal
-- credit, the amount before any reduction under regulation 81 or section 26 or 27 of the Act. Paragraph (2A): housing benefit is
-- nil. Paragraph (3): an employment and support allowance for which the person is disqualified by section 18 of the Welfare Reform
-- Act 2007 is disregarded as a welfare benefit, so counts nil. The order in which they are applied is fork F-C1.
-- src:1278 | (1) Subject to the following provisions of this regulation, the amount of a welfare benefit to be used when determining total entitlement to welfare benefits is the amount to which the single person or couple is entitled during the reference period subject to any adjustment to the amount payable in accordance with regulations under section 73 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992 (overlapping benefits).
-- src:1279 | (2) Where the welfare benefit is universal credit, the amount to be used is the amount to which the claimant is entitled before any reduction under regulation 81 or under section 26 or 27 of the Act.
-- src:1280 | (2A) Where the welfare benefit is housing benefit under section 130 of the Contributions and Benefits Act, the amount to be used is nil.
-- src:1281 | (3) Where a person is disqualified for receiving an employment and support allowance by virtue of section 18 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007, it is disregarded as a welfare benefit.
-- src:1282 | (4) Where an amount of a welfare benefit is taken into account in assessing a single person's or a couple's unearned income for the purposes of an award of universal credit the amount to be used is the amount taken into account as unearned income in accordance with regulation 66.
-- src:1283 | (5) Where a welfare benefit is awarded in respect of a period that is not a month, the amount is to be calculated as the monthly equivalent as set out in regulation 73 (unearned income calculated monthly).
@ref reg 80(1) to (5) (src:1278-1283)
GIVEN benefit IS A `Welfare benefit to which a person or couple is entitled during the reference period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 80 — the amount of a welfare benefit used` benefit MEANS
    `core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny`
        (CONSIDER benefit's kind
         WHEN `universal credit` THEN benefit's `amount of universal credit to which the claimant is entitled before any reduction under regulation 81 or under section 26 or 27 of the Act`
         WHEN `housing benefit under section 130 of the Contributions and Benefits Act` THEN 0
         WHEN `employment and support allowance for which the person is disqualified by virtue of section 18 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007` THEN 0
         WHEN `another welfare benefit` THEN
             CONSIDER benefit's `amount taken into account as unearned income in accordance with regulation 66`
             WHEN JUST counted THEN counted
             WHEN NOTHING THEN `core — the monthly equivalent of a payment` (benefit's `amount to which the person or couple is entitled for the period for which the benefit is awarded, after any adjustment in accordance with regulations under section 73 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992`) (benefit's `interval of the period for which the benefit is awarded`))

-- src:1277 | 80 Manner of determining total entitlement to welfare benefits
-- src:1278 | (1) Subject to the following provisions of this regulation, the amount of a welfare benefit to be used when determining total entitlement to welfare benefits is the amount to which the single person or couple is entitled during the reference period subject to any adjustment to the amount payable in accordance with regulations under section 73 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992 (overlapping benefits).
-- src:1279 | (2) Where the welfare benefit is universal credit, the amount to be used is the amount to which the claimant is entitled before any reduction under regulation 81 or under section 26 or 27 of the Act.
-- src:1280 | (2A) Where the welfare benefit is housing benefit under section 130 of the Contributions and Benefits Act, the amount to be used is nil.
-- src:1281 | (3) Where a person is disqualified for receiving an employment and support allowance by virtue of section 18 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007, it is disregarded as a welfare benefit.
-- src:1282 | (4) Where an amount of a welfare benefit is taken into account in assessing a single person's or a couple's unearned income for the purposes of an award of universal credit the amount to be used is the amount taken into account as unearned income in accordance with regulation 66.
-- src:1283 | (5) Where a welfare benefit is awarded in respect of a period that is not a month, the amount is to be calculated as the monthly equivalent as set out in regulation 73 (unearned income calculated monthly).
@ref reg 80 (src:1277-1283)
GIVEN benefits IS A LIST OF `Welfare benefit to which a person or couple is entitled during the reference period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 80 — the total entitlement to welfare benefits` benefits MEANS
    `core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny` (sum (map (GIVEN benefit YIELD `reg 80 — the amount of a welfare benefit used` benefit) benefits))

§§ `Regulation 80A -- Relevant amount`

-- src:1295 | (3) For the purposes of section 96 of the Act (benefit cap) and this regulation a claimant is resident in Greater London if—
-- src:1296 | (a) where the housing costs element is included in the claimant’s award of universal credit—
-- src:1297 | (i) accommodation in respect of which the claimant meets the occupation condition is in Greater London; or
-- src:1298 | (ii) the claimant is in receipt of housing benefit in respect of a dwelling (which has the meaning given in section 137 of the Contributions and Benefits Act) in Greater London;
-- src:1299 | (b) where the housing costs element is not included in the claimant’s award of universal credit—
-- src:1300 | (i) accommodation that the claimant normally occupies as their home is in Greater London; or
-- src:1301 | (ii) where there is no accommodation that the claimant normally occupies as their home, the Jobcentre Plus office to which the Secretary of State has allocated their claim is in Greater London.
@ref reg 80A(3) (src:1295-1301)
DECLARE `Accommodation of a claimant for regulation 80A(3)` HAS
    `the housing costs element is included in the claimant's award of universal credit`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `accommodation in respect of which the claimant meets the occupation condition is in Greater London`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant is in receipt of housing benefit in respect of a dwelling in Greater London`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is accommodation that the claimant normally occupies as their home`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `accommodation that the claimant normally occupies as their home is in Greater London`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Jobcentre Plus office to which the Secretary of State has allocated the claim is in Greater London`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- Paragraph (3): a claimant is resident in Greater London if (a) where the housing costs element is included in the award, the
-- accommodation for which the occupation condition (Schedule 3, a stated fact) is met is in Greater London, or the claimant receives
-- housing benefit for a dwelling in Greater London; (b) where it is not included, the accommodation the claimant normally occupies as
-- their home is in Greater London or, where there is none, the Jobcentre Plus office allocated to the claim is in Greater London.
-- src:1295 | (3) For the purposes of section 96 of the Act (benefit cap) and this regulation a claimant is resident in Greater London if—
-- src:1296 | (a) where the housing costs element is included in the claimant’s award of universal credit—
-- src:1297 | (i) accommodation in respect of which the claimant meets the occupation condition is in Greater London; or
-- src:1298 | (ii) the claimant is in receipt of housing benefit in respect of a dwelling (which has the meaning given in section 137 of the Contributions and Benefits Act) in Greater London;
-- src:1299 | (b) where the housing costs element is not included in the claimant’s award of universal credit—
-- src:1300 | (i) accommodation that the claimant normally occupies as their home is in Greater London; or
-- src:1301 | (ii) where there is no accommodation that the claimant normally occupies as their home, the Jobcentre Plus office to which the Secretary of State has allocated their claim is in Greater London.
@ref reg 80A(3) (src:1295-1301)
GIVEN accommodation IS AN `Accommodation of a claimant for regulation 80A(3)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 80A(3) — the claimant is resident in Greater London` accommodation MEANS
    IF accommodation's `the housing costs element is included in the claimant's award of universal credit`
    THEN (    (accommodation's `accommodation in respect of which the claimant meets the occupation condition is in Greater London`)
          OR  (accommodation's `the claimant is in receipt of housing benefit in respect of a dwelling in Greater London`))
    ELSE (IF accommodation's `there is accommodation that the claimant normally occupies as their home`
          THEN accommodation's `accommodation that the claimant normally occupies as their home is in Greater London`
          ELSE accommodation's `the Jobcentre Plus office to which the Secretary of State has allocated the claim is in Greater London`)

-- Paragraph (2): the applicable annual limit. "A single claimant" is read as covering both of the keel's single bases
-- (a single claimant, and a single claimant who is a member of a couple); joint claimants are the other basis (fork F-C2).
-- For joint claimants in Greater London, either of them being resident there is enough.
-- src:1286 | (2) The applicable annual limit is—
-- src:1287 | (a) £16,967 for a single claimant resident in Greater London who is not responsible for a child or qualifying young person;
-- src:1288 | (b) £25,323 for—
-- src:1289 | (i) joint claimants where either joint claimant is resident in Greater London;
-- src:1290 | (ii) a single claimant resident in Greater London who is responsible for a child or qualifying young person;
-- src:1291 | (c) £14,753 for a single claimant not resident in Greater London who is not responsible for a child or qualifying young person;
-- src:1292 | (d) £22,020 for—
-- src:1293 | (i) joint claimants not resident in Greater London;
-- src:1294 | (ii) a single claimant not resident in Greater London who is responsible for a child or qualifying young person.
@ref reg 80A(2) (src:1286-1294)
GIVEN basis IS A `Claim basis`
      `the claimant is resident in Greater London` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other joint claimant is resident in Greater London` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is responsible for a child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 80A(2) — the applicable annual limit` basis `the claimant is resident in Greater London` `the other joint claimant is resident in Greater London` `the claimant is responsible for a child or qualifying young person` MEANS
    CONSIDER basis
    WHEN `joint claimants` THEN
        IF (`the claimant is resident in Greater London`) OR (`the other joint claimant is resident in Greater London`)
        THEN 25323
        ELSE 22020
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the claimant is resident in Greater London`
        THEN (IF `the claimant is responsible for a child or qualifying young person` THEN 25323 ELSE 16967)
        ELSE (IF `the claimant is responsible for a child or qualifying young person` THEN 22020 ELSE 14753)

-- Paragraph (1): the relevant amount is the applicable annual limit divided by 12. It is rounded to the penny as regulation 6(1)
-- provides before it is compared with the benefits (fork F-C3).
-- src:1284 | 80A Relevant amount
-- src:1285 | (1) The relevant amount is determined by dividing the applicable annual limit by 12.
@ref reg 80A(1) (src:1284-1285)
GIVEN `applicable annual limit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 80A(1) — the relevant amount` `applicable annual limit` MEANS
    `core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny` (`applicable annual limit` DIVIDED BY 12)

§§ `Regulation 81 -- Reduction of universal credit`

-- Paragraph (3): the excess is the total amount of welfare benefits to which the single person or the couple are entitled in the
-- reference period, minus the relevant amount determined under regulation 80A.
-- src:1307 | (3) The excess is the total amount of welfare benefits that the single person or the couple are entitled to in the reference period, minus the relevant amount determined under regulation 80A.
@ref reg 81(3) (src:1307)
GIVEN `total welfare benefits to which the single person or couple is entitled during the reference period` IS A NUMBER
      `relevant amount determined under regulation 80A` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 81(3) — the excess` `total welfare benefits to which the single person or couple is entitled during the reference period` `relevant amount determined under regulation 80A` MEANS
    `core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny` (`total welfare benefits to which the single person or couple is entitled during the reference period` MINUS `relevant amount determined under regulation 80A`)

-- Paragraphs (1) and (2): where the cap applies, the award for the assessment period is reduced by the excess minus any amount
-- included in the award for the childcare costs element; but no reduction is applied where the childcare costs element is greater
-- than the excess.
-- src:1303 | (1) Where the benefit cap applies in relation to an assessment period for an award of universal credit, the amount of the award for that period is to be reduced by—
-- src:1304 | (a) the excess; minus
-- src:1305 | (b) any amount included in the award for the childcare costs element in relation to that assessment period.
-- src:1306 | (2) But no reduction is to be applied where the amount of the childcare costs element is greater than the excess.
@ref reg 81(1) and (2) (src:1303-1306)
GIVEN `the benefit cap applies in relation to the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN
      excess IS A NUMBER
      `amount included in the award for the childcare costs element in relation to the assessment period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 81(1) and (2) — the reduction of the award` `the benefit cap applies in relation to the assessment period` excess `amount included in the award for the childcare costs element in relation to the assessment period` MEANS
    IF `the benefit cap applies in relation to the assessment period`
    THEN `core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny` (max 0 (excess MINUS `amount included in the award for the childcare costs element in relation to the assessment period`))
    ELSE 0

-- The amount of the award after the reduction. The text does not say what happens when the reduction is more than the award, so
-- there the result is NOTHING (fork F-C4).
-- src:1303 | (1) Where the benefit cap applies in relation to an assessment period for an award of universal credit, the amount of the award for that period is to be reduced by—
@ref reg 81(1) (src:1303)
GIVEN `amount of the award before the reduction` IS A NUMBER
      reduction IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 81(1) — the amount of the award after the reduction` `amount of the award before the reduction` reduction MEANS
    IF reduction AT MOST `amount of the award before the reduction`
    THEN JUST (`core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny` (`amount of the award before the reduction` MINUS reduction))
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 82 -- Exceptions: earnings`

-- Paragraph (1)(a): the claimant's earned income (or the couple's combined earned income) equals or exceeds the amount a person
-- would be paid at the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for 16 hours a week, converted to a
-- month by multiplying by 52 and dividing by 12 (the keel's weekly table does exactly that); the fraction of a pound is
-- disregarded (regulation 6(1A)(za)). Paragraph (5): the hourly rate is that in force at the beginning of the assessment period or
-- month for which the amount is calculated. Paragraph (4): earned income does not include income treated as had by regulation 62.
-- src:1310 | (a) the claimant's earned income or, if the claimant is a member of a couple, the couple's combined earned income, is equal to or exceeds the amount of earnings that a person would be paid at the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for 16 hours per week, converted to a monthly amount by multiplying by 52 and dividing by 12; or
@ref reg 82(1)(a) (src:1310)
GIVEN `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the assessment period or month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 82(1)(a) — the earnings threshold` `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the assessment period or month` MEANS
    `core — an amount with any fraction of a pound disregarded`
        (`core — the monthly equivalent of a payment` (`hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the assessment period or month` TIMES 16) `weekly payments`)

-- src:1310 | (a) the claimant's earned income or, if the claimant is a member of a couple, the couple's combined earned income, is equal to or exceeds the amount of earnings that a person would be paid at the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for 16 hours per week, converted to a monthly amount by multiplying by 52 and dividing by 12; or
@ref reg 82(1)(a) (src:1310)
GIVEN `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS A NUMBER
      `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the assessment period or month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 82(1)(a) — the earned income equals or exceeds the earnings threshold` `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the assessment period or month` MEANS
    `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` AT LEAST `reg 82(1)(a) — the earnings threshold` `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the assessment period or month`

-- src:1317 | (3) The condition is that, in each of the 12 months immediately preceding that day, the claimant's earned income or, if the claimant was a member of a couple, the couple's combined earned income was equal to or exceeded—
-- src:1318 | (a) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:1319 | (b) ...the amount calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(a).
-- src:1320 | (4) “Earned income” for the purposes of this regulation does not include income a person is treated as having by virtue of regulation 62 (minimum income floor).
-- src:1321 | (5) For the purposes of paragraphs (2)(a) and (3), when calculating the amount in accordance with paragraph (1)(a) the reference to regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations is a reference to regulation 4 as in force at the beginning of the assessment period or month for which the amount is calculated.
@ref reg 82(3) and (5) (src:1317-1321)
DECLARE `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin` HAS
    `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62`  IS A NUMBER
    `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month`  IS A NUMBER

-- Paragraph (3): the condition is that in each of the 12 months immediately preceding the day, the claimant's (or couple's) earned
-- income was equal to or exceeded the amount calculated in accordance with (1)(a). (3)(a) is a run of dots in this text. Fewer than
-- 12 months of evidence means the condition is not shown to be met.
-- src:1317 | (3) The condition is that, in each of the 12 months immediately preceding that day, the claimant's earned income or, if the claimant was a member of a couple, the couple's combined earned income was equal to or exceeded—
-- src:1318 | (a) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:1319 | (b) ...the amount calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(a).
@ref reg 82(3) (src:1317-1319)
GIVEN months IS A LIST OF `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 82(3) — the condition is met` months MEANS
        (count months EQUALS 12)
    AND (all (GIVEN month YIELD `reg 82(1)(a) — the earned income equals or exceeds the earnings threshold` (month's `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, in the month, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62`) (month's `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the month`)) months)

-- src:1312 | (2) A grace period is a period of 9 consecutive months that begins on the most recent of the following days in respect of which the condition in paragraph (3) is met—
-- src:1313 | (a) a day falling within the current period of entitlement to universal credit which is the first day of an assessment period in which the claimant's earned income (or, if the claimant is a member of a couple, the couple's combined earned income) is less than—
-- src:1314 | (i) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:1315 | (ii) ...the amount calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(a);
-- src:1316 | (b) a day falling before the current period of entitlement to universal credit which is the day after a day on which the claimant has ceased paid work.
@ref reg 82(2) (src:1312-1316)
DECLARE `Day on which a grace period may begin` HAS
    day                                                                                      IS A DATE
    `the day falls within the current period of entitlement to universal credit`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day is the first day of an assessment period`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `earned income in that assessment period, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62`  IS A NUMBER
    `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of that assessment period`  IS A NUMBER
    `the day falls before the current period of entitlement to universal credit`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant ceased paid work on the day before`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the 12 months immediately preceding that day`                                           IS A LIST OF `Month before a day on which a grace period may begin`

-- src:1313 | (a) a day falling within the current period of entitlement to universal credit which is the first day of an assessment period in which the claimant's earned income (or, if the claimant is a member of a couple, the couple's combined earned income) is less than—
-- src:1314 | (i) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:1315 | (ii) ...the amount calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(a);
@ref reg 82(2)(a) (src:1313-1315)
GIVEN candidate IS A `Day on which a grace period may begin`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 82(2)(a) — the day is the first day of an assessment period with earned income below the threshold` candidate MEANS
        (candidate's `the day falls within the current period of entitlement to universal credit`)
    AND (candidate's `the day is the first day of an assessment period`)
    AND (NOT (`reg 82(1)(a) — the earned income equals or exceeds the earnings threshold` (candidate's `earned income in that assessment period, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62`) (candidate's `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of that assessment period`)))

-- src:1316 | (b) a day falling before the current period of entitlement to universal credit which is the day after a day on which the claimant has ceased paid work.
@ref reg 82(2)(b) (src:1316)
GIVEN candidate IS A `Day on which a grace period may begin`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 82(2)(b) — the day is the day after the claimant ceased paid work` candidate MEANS
        (candidate's `the day falls before the current period of entitlement to universal credit`)
    AND (candidate's `the claimant ceased paid work on the day before`)

-- src:1312 | (2) A grace period is a period of 9 consecutive months that begins on the most recent of the following days in respect of which the condition in paragraph (3) is met—
-- src:1313 | (a) a day falling within the current period of entitlement to universal credit which is the first day of an assessment period in which the claimant's earned income (or, if the claimant is a member of a couple, the couple's combined earned income) is less than—
-- src:1314 | (i) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:1315 | (ii) ...the amount calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(a);
-- src:1316 | (b) a day falling before the current period of entitlement to universal credit which is the day after a day on which the claimant has ceased paid work.
-- src:1317 | (3) The condition is that, in each of the 12 months immediately preceding that day, the claimant's earned income or, if the claimant was a member of a couple, the couple's combined earned income was equal to or exceeded—
-- src:1318 | (a) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:1319 | (b) ...the amount calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(a).
@ref reg 82(2) and (3) (src:1312-1319)
GIVEN candidate IS A `Day on which a grace period may begin`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 82(2) — a grace period may begin on the day` candidate MEANS
        (    (`reg 82(2)(a) — the day is the first day of an assessment period with earned income below the threshold` candidate)
         OR  (`reg 82(2)(b) — the day is the day after the claimant ceased paid work` candidate))
    AND (`reg 82(3) — the condition is met` (candidate's `the 12 months immediately preceding that day`))

-- Paragraph (2): a grace period begins on the most recent of the days on which a grace period may begin. The days considered are
-- those not later than the last day of the assessment period asked about (fork F-C5).
-- src:1312 | (2) A grace period is a period of 9 consecutive months that begins on the most recent of the following days in respect of which the condition in paragraph (3) is met—
@ref reg 82(2) (src:1312)
GIVEN dates IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`reg 82(2) — the latest of the days` dates MEANS
    CONSIDER dates
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN date FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER `reg 82(2) — the latest of the days` rest
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST date
        WHEN JUST latest THEN JUST (IF date AT LEAST latest THEN date ELSE latest)

-- src:1312 | (2) A grace period is a period of 9 consecutive months that begins on the most recent of the following days in respect of which the condition in paragraph (3) is met—
@ref reg 82(2) (src:1312)
GIVEN candidates IS A LIST OF `Day on which a grace period may begin`
      period IS AN `Assessment period`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`reg 82(2) — the day on which the grace period begins` candidates period MEANS
    `reg 82(2) — the latest of the days`
        (map (GIVEN candidate YIELD candidate's day)
             (filter (GIVEN candidate YIELD (`reg 82(2) — a grace period may begin on the day` candidate) AND (candidate's day AT MOST period's `last day`)) candidates))

DECLARE `Grace period` HAS
    `first day of the grace period`   IS A DATE
    `last day of the grace period`    IS A DATE

-- A grace period is nine consecutive months from that day: it ends on the day before the ninth monthly anniversary (fork F-C6).
-- src:1312 | (2) A grace period is a period of 9 consecutive months that begins on the most recent of the following days in respect of which the condition in paragraph (3) is met—
@ref reg 82(2) (src:1312)
GIVEN candidates IS A LIST OF `Day on which a grace period may begin`
      period IS AN `Assessment period`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Grace period`
`reg 82(2) — the grace period` candidates period MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 82(2) — the day on which the grace period begins` candidates period
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST begins THEN
        JUST (`Grace period` WITH
                `first day of the grace period` IS begins
                `last day of the grace period` IS (`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` begins (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 9, unit IS months)) PLUS (0 MINUS 1))

-- Paragraph (1)(b): the assessment period falls within a grace period, or is an assessment period in which a grace period begins or
-- ends.
-- src:1311 | (b) the assessment period falls within a grace period or is an assessment period in which a grace period begins or ends.
@ref reg 82(1)(b) (src:1311)
GIVEN grace IS A `Grace period`
      period IS AN `Assessment period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 82(1)(b) — the assessment period is within a grace period or one in which it begins or ends` grace period MEANS
        ((grace's `first day of the grace period` AT MOST period's `first day`) AND (period's `last day` AT MOST grace's `last day of the grace period`))
    OR  ((period's `first day` AT MOST grace's `first day of the grace period`) AND (grace's `first day of the grace period` AT MOST period's `last day`))
    OR  ((period's `first day` AT MOST grace's `last day of the grace period`) AND (grace's `last day of the grace period` AT MOST period's `last day`))

-- Paragraph (1): the benefit cap does not apply to an award of universal credit in relation to an assessment period where (a) the
-- earned income is at least the threshold, or (b) the assessment period is within a grace period or one in which it begins or ends.
-- src:1309 | (1) The benefit cap does not apply to an award of universal credit in relation to an assessment period where—
-- src:1310 | (a) the claimant's earned income or, if the claimant is a member of a couple, the couple's combined earned income, is equal to or exceeds the amount of earnings that a person would be paid at the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for 16 hours per week, converted to a monthly amount by multiplying by 52 and dividing by 12; or
-- src:1311 | (b) the assessment period falls within a grace period or is an assessment period in which a grace period begins or ends.
@ref reg 82(1) (src:1309-1311)
GIVEN `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` IS A NUMBER
      `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the assessment period or month` IS A NUMBER
      candidates IS A LIST OF `Day on which a grace period may begin`
      period IS AN `Assessment period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 82(1) — the benefit cap does not apply by reason of earnings` `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the assessment period or month` candidates period MEANS
        (`reg 82(1)(a) — the earned income equals or exceeds the earnings threshold` `earned income of the claimant, or the couple's combined earned income, not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62` `hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations as in force at the beginning of the assessment period or month`)
    OR  (CONSIDER `reg 82(2) — the grace period` candidates period
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST grace THEN `reg 82(1)(b) — the assessment period is within a grace period or one in which it begins or ends` grace period)

§§ `Regulation 82(4) and (5) -- Notes on earned income and the rate (carried by the rules above)`
-- src:1320 | (4) “Earned income” for the purposes of this regulation does not include income a person is treated as having by virtue of regulation 62 (minimum income floor).
-- src:1321 | (5) For the purposes of paragraphs (2)(a) and (3), when calculating the amount in accordance with paragraph (1)(a) the reference to regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations is a reference to regulation 4 as in force at the beginning of the assessment period or month for which the amount is calculated.
-- Paragraph (4) is carried by the field names (`not including income treated as had by virtue of regulation 62`); paragraph (5) by
-- the field names that fix the rate as the one in force at the beginning of the assessment period or month.

§§ `Regulation 83(2) -- "war pension"`

-- src:1348 | (2) For the purposes of this regulation, “war pension” means—
-- src:1349 | (a) any pension or allowance payable under any of the instruments listed in section 639(2) of ITEPA—
-- src:1350 | (i) to a widow, widower or a surviving civil partner, or
-- src:1351 | (ii) in respect of disablement;
-- src:1352 | (b) a pension payable to a person as a widow, widower or surviving civil partner under any power of Her Majesty otherwise than under an enactment to make provision about pensions for or in respect of persons who have been disabled or have died in consequence of service as members of the armed forces of the Crown;
-- src:1353 | (c) a payment which is made under any of—
-- src:1354 | (i) the Order in Council of 19th December 1881,
-- src:1355 | (ii) the Royal Warrant of 27th October 1884, or
-- src:1356 | (iii) the Order by His Majesty of 14th January 1922,
-- src:1357 | to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner of a person whose death was attributable to service in a capacity analogous to service as a member of the armed forces of the Crown and whose service in such capacity terminated before 31st March 1973;
-- src:1358 | (d) a pension paid by the government of a country outside the United Kingdom which is analogous to any of the pensions, allowances or payments mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (c).
@ref reg 83(2) (src:1348-1358)
DECLARE `Pension that may be a war pension` HAS
    `pension or allowance payable under an instrument listed in section 639(2) of ITEPA`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `payable to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `payable in respect of disablement`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `pension payable to a person as a widow, widower or surviving civil partner under a power of the Crown to make provision about pensions for or in respect of persons who have been disabled or have died in consequence of service as members of the armed forces of the Crown`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `provision under which the pension is paid`                                               IS A `Provision whose standing as an enactment is asked by uc2`
    `payment made under the Order in Council of 19th December 1881, the Royal Warrant of 27th October 1884 or the Order by His Majesty of 14th January 1922`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `payable to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner of a person whose death was attributable to service in a capacity analogous to service as a member of the armed forces of the Crown`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `date on which that person's service in such a capacity terminated`                       IS A MAYBE DATE
    `pension paid by the government of a country outside the United Kingdom which is analogous to a pension, allowance or payment mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (c)`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1349 | (a) any pension or allowance payable under any of the instruments listed in section 639(2) of ITEPA—
-- src:1350 | (i) to a widow, widower or a surviving civil partner, or
-- src:1351 | (ii) in respect of disablement;
@ref reg 83(2)(a) (src:1349-1351)
GIVEN pension IS A `Pension that may be a war pension`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 83(2)(a) — a pension or allowance under a listed instrument` pension MEANS
        (pension's `pension or allowance payable under an instrument listed in section 639(2) of ITEPA`)
    AND (    (pension's `payable to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner`)
          OR (pension's `payable in respect of disablement`))

-- src:1352 | (b) a pension payable to a person as a widow, widower or surviving civil partner under any power of Her Majesty otherwise than under an enactment to make provision about pensions for or in respect of persons who have been disabled or have died in consequence of service as members of the armed forces of the Crown;
@ref reg 83(2)(b) (src:1352)
GIVEN pension IS A `Pension that may be a war pension`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 83(2)(b) — a pension under a power of the Crown otherwise than under an enactment` pension MEANS
        (pension's `pension payable to a person as a widow, widower or surviving civil partner under a power of the Crown to make provision about pensions for or in respect of persons who have been disabled or have died in consequence of service as members of the armed forces of the Crown`)
    AND (NOT (`uc2 helper — a provision is an enactment` (pension's `provision under which the pension is paid`)))

-- src:1353 | (c) a payment which is made under any of—
-- src:1354 | (i) the Order in Council of 19th December 1881,
-- src:1355 | (ii) the Royal Warrant of 27th October 1884, or
-- src:1356 | (iii) the Order by His Majesty of 14th January 1922,
-- src:1357 | to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner of a person whose death was attributable to service in a capacity analogous to service as a member of the armed forces of the Crown and whose service in such capacity terminated before 31st March 1973;
@ref reg 83(2)(c) (src:1353-1357)
GIVEN pension IS A `Pension that may be a war pension`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 83(2)(c) — a payment under one of the three instruments to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner` pension MEANS
        (pension's `payment made under the Order in Council of 19th December 1881, the Royal Warrant of 27th October 1884 or the Order by His Majesty of 14th January 1922`)
    AND (pension's `payable to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner of a person whose death was attributable to service in a capacity analogous to service as a member of the armed forces of the Crown`)
    AND (CONSIDER pension's `date on which that person's service in such a capacity terminated`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST terminated THEN terminated LESS THAN YearMonthDay 1973 3 31)

-- src:1348 | (2) For the purposes of this regulation, “war pension” means—
-- src:1349 | (a) any pension or allowance payable under any of the instruments listed in section 639(2) of ITEPA—
-- src:1350 | (i) to a widow, widower or a surviving civil partner, or
-- src:1351 | (ii) in respect of disablement;
-- src:1352 | (b) a pension payable to a person as a widow, widower or surviving civil partner under any power of Her Majesty otherwise than under an enactment to make provision about pensions for or in respect of persons who have been disabled or have died in consequence of service as members of the armed forces of the Crown;
-- src:1353 | (c) a payment which is made under any of—
-- src:1354 | (i) the Order in Council of 19th December 1881,
-- src:1355 | (ii) the Royal Warrant of 27th October 1884, or
-- src:1356 | (iii) the Order by His Majesty of 14th January 1922,
-- src:1357 | to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner of a person whose death was attributable to service in a capacity analogous to service as a member of the armed forces of the Crown and whose service in such capacity terminated before 31st March 1973;
-- src:1358 | (d) a pension paid by the government of a country outside the United Kingdom which is analogous to any of the pensions, allowances or payments mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (c).
@ref reg 83(2) (src:1348-1358)
GIVEN pension IS A `Pension that may be a war pension`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 83(2) — war pension` pension MEANS
        (`reg 83(2)(a) — a pension or allowance under a listed instrument` pension)
    OR  (`reg 83(2)(b) — a pension under a power of the Crown otherwise than under an enactment` pension)
    OR  (`reg 83(2)(c) — a payment under one of the three instruments to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner` pension)
    OR  (pension's `pension paid by the government of a country outside the United Kingdom which is analogous to a pension, allowance or payment mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (c)`)

§§ `Regulation 83(1) -- Exceptions: entitlement or receipt of certain benefits`

-- src:1322 | 83 Exceptions - entitlement or receipt of certain benefits
-- src:1323 | (1) The benefit cap does not apply in relation to any assessment period where—
-- src:1324 | (a) the LCWRA element is included in the award of universal credit or the claimant is receiving an employment and support allowance that includes the support component;
-- src:1325 | (b) a claimant is receiving industrial injuries benefit;
-- src:1326 | (c) a claimant is receiving attendance allowance;
-- src:1327 | (ca) a claimant is receiving pension age disability payment;
-- src:1328 | (d) a claimant is receiving a war pension;
-- src:1329 | (e) a claimant is receiving a payment under article 15(1)(c) or article 29(1)(a) of the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011;
-- src:1330 | (f) a claimant, or a child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible, is receiving disability living allowance;
-- src:1331 | (fa) a claimant, or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible, is receiving Scottish adult disability living allowance;
-- src:1332 | (g) a claimant, or a qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible, is receiving personal independence payment;
-- src:1333 | (h) a claimant, or a child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible, is entitled to a payment listed in sub-paragraphs (b) to (g) , (ha) or (hb) but—
-- src:1334 | (i) is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 6 (hospitalisation) or regulation 7 (persons in care homes) of the Social Security (Attendance Allowance) Regulations 1991,
-- src:1335 | (ii) it is being withheld by virtue of article 53 of the Naval, Military and Air Forces etc (Disablement and Death) Service Pensions Order 2006 (maintenance in hospital or an institution),
-- src:1336 | (iii) is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 8 (hospitalisation) or regulation 9 (persons in care homes) of the Social Security (Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 1991, ...
-- src:1337 | (iv) in the case of personal independence payment, is not receiving it by virtue of regulations under section 85 (care home residents) or 86 (hospital in-patients) of the Act.
-- src:1338 | (iva) in the case of adult disability payment, is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 27 (effect of admission to a care home on ongoing entitlement to daily living component) or 28 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Adult Disability Payment) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022, ...
-- src:1339 | (v) is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 17 (effect of admission to a care home on ongoing entitlement to care component) of the DACYP Regulations; ...
-- src:1340 | (vi) in the case of pension age disability payment, is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 19 (effect of admission to a care home on ongoing entitlement to pension age disability payment) or regulation 20 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to pension age disability payment) of the Disability Assistance for Older People (Scotland) Regulations 2024; or
-- src:1341 | (vii) in the case of Scottish adult disability living allowance, is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 22 (effect of admission to a care home on ongoing entitlement to care component) or regulation 23 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Scottish adult disability living allowance) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025;
-- src:1342 | (ha) a claimant, or a child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible, is receiving child disability payment;
-- src:1343 | (hb) a claimant, or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible, is receiving adult disability payment;
-- src:1344 | (i) a claimant, or a qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible, is entitled to carer’s allowance;
-- src:1345 | (ia) a claimant, or a qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible, is entitled to carer support payment;
-- src:1346 | (j) the carer element is included in the award of universal credit;
-- src:1347 | (k) a claimant is entitled to guardian’s allowance under section 77 of the Contributions and Benefits Act.
@ref reg 83(1) (src:1322-1347)
DECLARE `Person in the household` IS ONE OF
    `a claimant`
    `a child for whom a claimant is responsible`
    `a qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible`

