-- src:1335 | (ii) it is being withheld by virtue of article 53 of the Naval, Military and Air Forces etc (Disablement and Death) Service Pensions Order 2006 (maintenance in hospital or an institution),
-- src:1336 | (iii) is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 8 (hospitalisation) or regulation 9 (persons in care homes) of the Social Security (Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 1991, ...
-- src:1337 | (iv) in the case of personal independence payment, is not receiving it by virtue of regulations under section 85 (care home residents) or 86 (hospital in-patients) of the Act.
-- src:1338 | (iva) in the case of adult disability payment, is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 27 (effect of admission to a care home on ongoing entitlement to daily living component) or 28 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Adult Disability Payment) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022, ...
-- src:1339 | (v) is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 17 (effect of admission to a care home on ongoing entitlement to care component) of the DACYP Regulations; ...
-- src:1340 | (vi) in the case of pension age disability payment, is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 19 (effect of admission to a care home on ongoing entitlement to pension age disability payment) or regulation 20 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to pension age disability payment) of the Disability Assistance for Older People (Scotland) Regulations 2024; or
-- src:1341 | (vii) in the case of Scottish adult disability living allowance, is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 22 (effect of admission to a care home on ongoing entitlement to care component) or regulation 23 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Scottish adult disability living allowance) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025;
-- src:1342 | (ha) a claimant, or a child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible, is receiving child disability payment;
-- src:1343 | (hb) a claimant, or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible, is receiving adult disability payment;
-- src:1344 | (i) a claimant, or a qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible, is entitled to carer’s allowance;
-- src:1345 | (ia) a claimant, or a qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible, is entitled to carer support payment;
-- src:1346 | (j) the carer element is included in the award of universal credit;
-- src:1347 | (k) a claimant is entitled to guardian’s allowance under section 77 of the Contributions and Benefits Act.
@ref reg 83(1) (src:1322-1347)
DECLARE `Household for regulation 83` HAS
    members                                                                                   IS A LIST OF `Member of the household for regulation 83`
    `the LCWRA element is included in the award of universal credit`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `a claimant is receiving an employment and support allowance that includes the support component`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carer element is included in the award of universal credit`                          IS A BOOLEAN

-- A payment of the kind "a war pension" counts only if the pension is a war pension as paragraph (2) defines it.
-- src:1348 | (2) For the purposes of this regulation, “war pension” means—
@ref reg 83(2) (src:1348)
GIVEN item IS A `Payment to a person for regulation 83`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 83 — the payment is of the kind it is said to be` item MEANS
    IF item's payment EQUALS `a war pension`
    THEN `reg 83(2) — war pension` (item's pension)
    ELSE TRUE

DECLARE `Persons whose payments are asked about` IS ONE OF
    `a claimant`
    `a claimant or a qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible`
    `a claimant, or a child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible`

GIVEN member IS A `Member of the household for regulation 83`
      persons IS A `Persons whose payments are asked about`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 83 — the member is one of the persons asked about` member persons MEANS
    CONSIDER persons
    WHEN `a claimant` THEN member's role EQUALS `a claimant`
    WHEN `a claimant or a qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible` THEN
        (member's role EQUALS `a claimant`) OR (member's role EQUALS `a qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible`)
    WHEN `a claimant, or a child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible` THEN TRUE

GIVEN household IS A `Household for regulation 83`
      kind IS A `Payment named in regulation 83`
      persons IS A `Persons whose payments are asked about`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 83 — one of the persons is receiving the payment` household kind persons MEANS
    any (GIVEN member YIELD
            (`reg 83 — the member is one of the persons asked about` member persons)
            AND (any (GIVEN item YIELD
                        ((item's payment) EQUALS kind)
                        AND ((item's position) EQUALS `receiving it`)
                        AND (`reg 83 — the payment is of the kind it is said to be` item))
                     (member's payments)))
        (household's members)

GIVEN household IS A `Household for regulation 83`
      kind IS A `Payment named in regulation 83`
      persons IS A `Persons whose payments are asked about`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 83 — one of the persons is entitled to the payment` household kind persons MEANS
    any (GIVEN member YIELD
            (`reg 83 — the member is one of the persons asked about` member persons)
            AND (any (GIVEN item YIELD
                        ((item's payment) EQUALS kind)
                        AND (NOT ((item's position) EQUALS `neither entitled to it nor receiving it`))
                        AND (`reg 83 — the payment is of the kind it is said to be` item))
                     (member's payments)))
        (household's members)

-- Sub-paragraph (h): a claimant, or a child or qualifying young person, is entitled to a payment listed in (b) to (g), (ha) or (hb)
-- but is not receiving it (or it is withheld) for one of the reasons (i) to (vii). The listed payments are industrial injuries
-- benefit, attendance allowance, pension age disability payment, a war pension, the payment under the 2011 Order, disability living
-- allowance, Scottish adult disability living allowance, personal independence payment, child disability payment
-- and adult disability payment.
-- src:1333 | (h) a claimant, or a child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible, is entitled to a payment listed in sub-paragraphs (b) to (g) , (ha) or (hb) but—
-- src:1334 | (i) is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 6 (hospitalisation) or regulation 7 (persons in care homes) of the Social Security (Attendance Allowance) Regulations 1991,
-- src:1335 | (ii) it is being withheld by virtue of article 53 of the Naval, Military and Air Forces etc (Disablement and Death) Service Pensions Order 2006 (maintenance in hospital or an institution),
-- src:1336 | (iii) is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 8 (hospitalisation) or regulation 9 (persons in care homes) of the Social Security (Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 1991, ...
-- src:1337 | (iv) in the case of personal independence payment, is not receiving it by virtue of regulations under section 85 (care home residents) or 86 (hospital in-patients) of the Act.
-- src:1338 | (iva) in the case of adult disability payment, is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 27 (effect of admission to a care home on ongoing entitlement to daily living component) or 28 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Adult Disability Payment) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022, ...
-- src:1339 | (v) is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 17 (effect of admission to a care home on ongoing entitlement to care component) of the DACYP Regulations; ...
-- src:1340 | (vi) in the case of pension age disability payment, is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 19 (effect of admission to a care home on ongoing entitlement to pension age disability payment) or regulation 20 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to pension age disability payment) of the Disability Assistance for Older People (Scotland) Regulations 2024; or
-- src:1341 | (vii) in the case of Scottish adult disability living allowance, is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 22 (effect of admission to a care home on ongoing entitlement to care component) or regulation 23 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Scottish adult disability living allowance) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025;
@ref reg 83(1)(h) (src:1333-1341)
GIVEN kind IS A `Payment named in regulation 83`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 83(1)(h) — the payment is one listed in sub-paragraphs (b) to (g), (ha) or (hb)` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `industrial injuries benefit` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `attendance allowance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `pension age disability payment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a war pension` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a payment under article 15(1)(c) or article 29(1)(a) of the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `disability living allowance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Scottish adult disability living allowance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `personal independence payment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `child disability payment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `adult disability payment` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN item IS A `Payment to a person for regulation 83`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 83(1)(h) — the position is one of the reasons for not receiving it` item MEANS
    CONSIDER item's position
    WHEN `entitled to it but not receiving it by virtue of regulation 6 or regulation 7 of the Social Security (Attendance Allowance) Regulations 1991` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `entitled to it but withheld by virtue of article 53 of the Naval, Military and Air Forces etc (Disablement and Death) Service Pensions Order 2006` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `entitled to it but not receiving it by virtue of regulation 8 or regulation 9 of the Social Security (Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 1991` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `entitled to it but not receiving it by virtue of regulations under section 85 or 86 of the Act` THEN item's payment EQUALS `personal independence payment`
    WHEN `entitled to it but not receiving it by virtue of regulation 27 or 28 of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022` THEN item's payment EQUALS `adult disability payment`
    WHEN `entitled to it but not receiving it by virtue of regulation 17 of the DACYP Regulations` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `entitled to it but not receiving it by virtue of regulation 19 or 20 of the Disability Assistance for Older People (Scotland) Regulations 2024` THEN item's payment EQUALS `pension age disability payment`
    WHEN `entitled to it but not receiving it by virtue of regulation 22 or 23 of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025` THEN item's payment EQUALS `Scottish adult disability living allowance`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:1333 | (h) a claimant, or a child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible, is entitled to a payment listed in sub-paragraphs (b) to (g) , (ha) or (hb) but—
-- src:1334 | (i) is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 6 (hospitalisation) or regulation 7 (persons in care homes) of the Social Security (Attendance Allowance) Regulations 1991,
-- src:1335 | (ii) it is being withheld by virtue of article 53 of the Naval, Military and Air Forces etc (Disablement and Death) Service Pensions Order 2006 (maintenance in hospital or an institution),
-- src:1336 | (iii) is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 8 (hospitalisation) or regulation 9 (persons in care homes) of the Social Security (Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 1991, ...
-- src:1337 | (iv) in the case of personal independence payment, is not receiving it by virtue of regulations under section 85 (care home residents) or 86 (hospital in-patients) of the Act.
-- src:1338 | (iva) in the case of adult disability payment, is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 27 (effect of admission to a care home on ongoing entitlement to daily living component) or 28 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Adult Disability Payment) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022, ...
-- src:1339 | (v) is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 17 (effect of admission to a care home on ongoing entitlement to care component) of the DACYP Regulations; ...
-- src:1340 | (vi) in the case of pension age disability payment, is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 19 (effect of admission to a care home on ongoing entitlement to pension age disability payment) or regulation 20 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to pension age disability payment) of the Disability Assistance for Older People (Scotland) Regulations 2024; or
-- src:1341 | (vii) in the case of Scottish adult disability living allowance, is not receiving it by virtue of regulation 22 (effect of admission to a care home on ongoing entitlement to care component) or regulation 23 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Scottish adult disability living allowance) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025;
@ref reg 83(1)(h) (src:1333-1341)
GIVEN household IS A `Household for regulation 83`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 83(1)(h) — someone is entitled to a listed payment but is not receiving it for one of the reasons` household MEANS
    any (GIVEN member YIELD
            any (GIVEN item YIELD
                    (`reg 83(1)(h) — the payment is one listed in sub-paragraphs (b) to (g), (ha) or (hb)` (item's payment))
                    AND (`reg 83(1)(h) — the position is one of the reasons for not receiving it` item)
                    AND (`reg 83 — the payment is of the kind it is said to be` item))
                (member's payments))
        (household's members)

-- Sub-paragraphs (a) to (k).
